#==============================================================================================
#
#   webview - embedding the engine in an application: LibWebView and WebContent, in process
#
#   DESCRIPTION:
#       Ladybird splits embedding a page into two halves joined by IPC: LibWebView
#       (Libraries/LibWebView: ViewImplementation, the Application's process-wide setup,
#       URL.cpp's sanitize_url, SearchEngine, ErrorHTML.h) in the UI process, and WebContent
#       (Services/WebContent: PageHost, PageClient, ConnectionFromClient's input queue) in a
#       process per tab. The port runs the page in the application's process, so this module
#       holds the parts of both that apply, with each IPC message a direct call:
#
#           event_loop.lucb     the Core event loop over an embedder's run loop (the adapter of
#                               UI/AppKit's EventLoopImplementationMacOS): timers and deferred
#                               invocations, a wake hook, pumping without blocking
#           roots.lucb          C-heap memory the collector scans (GC::ConservativeVector)
#           resources.lucb      the resource:// files the loader reads, written once
#           platform.lucb       what WebContent's main and LibWebView's Application install
#           search_engine.lucb  SearchEngine.cpp
#           url.lucb            URL.cpp: sanitize_url, location_looks_like_url
#           error_page.lucb     ErrorHTML.h and ViewImplementation::load_navigation_error_page
#           page_client.lucb    WebContent::PageClient (and PageHost's page)
#           view.lucb           ViewImplementation and WebContentClient: loading, history,
#                               viewport, what the page reported
#           view_input.lucb     ViewImplementation::enqueue_input_event and
#                               ConnectionFromClient's input queue
#           view_pixels.lucb    the presented frame: server_did_paint and its pixels
#           view_gpu.lucb       the presented display list drawn by the GPU player
#           api.lucb            the functions a Luce application calls
#           tests_*.lucb        the module's tests
#
#       Every function that reaches the engine runs with the main thread VM's heap as the
#       current allocator (DESIGN.md §3.3), and memory this module keeps in the C heap is a
#       conservative root region (roots.lucb), so the managed values it holds stay alive.
#
#       Copyright (c) 2020-2026, the Ladybird developers.
#       Copyright (c) 2026 the luce-browser authors.
#       SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause (see LICENSE)
#
#==============================================================================================

